# What `project/agents.py` rendered for each type before the standing briefs moved out of its string
# literals and into `assets/toolkit/agents/`, as SHA-256 over the UTF-8 bytes of each generated file.
#
# The move is only worth doing if it changed nothing a project receives, and "generate before and after"
# cannot be run across one commit. So these were captured by running the generator at fee9ce4, the commit
# this change was written on top of, and the new path has to reproduce them exactly
# (`tests/test_briefs.py`). Anyone can take the same reading: check out fee9ce4, run
#
#     PYTHONPATH=src python3 -c "import hashlib; from slipwai.layout import Layout; \
#         from slipwai.project.agents import agent_files; \
#         print('\n'.join(f'{hashlib.sha256(t.encode()).hexdigest()}  {d}  {p}' \
#             for d in ('.', 'delivery') for p, t in sorted(agent_files(Layout(d)).items())))"
#
# and compare it with the lines below.
#
# Two layouts, because the one value a brief interpolates on every type that has it is `{{make}}`, and a
# project that keeps its delivery material in a subdirectory says `make -f delivery/Makefile`. A record
# taken at the default layout alone would pass with the substitution stubbed out to the empty string.
#
# A deliberate edit to a brief changes these, which is the point: the line a reviewer has to see change is
# the one saying which file's bytes a wording change moved. Re-read them the same way after the edit, with
# `agent_files` on the edited tree, and say in the commit which type was reworded.
#
# <sha256>  <project.json layout.delivery>  <path in the generated project>
#
# Re-taken for the `/drive` -> `/sail` rename, which moved every line at once: eleven file names and the
# command each brief names inside itself. That is the one kind of change this record cannot tell from a
# regression, so it is said here rather than left to be inferred from a diff of twenty-two digests. The
# claim above — that the move out of `agents.py` changed nothing — is now history rather than something
# these lines still prove; what they prove from here is that nothing changes a brief without saying so.
#
# Re-taken for the scheduling rules — two bands, a state per slice, refill at every boundary, a `question`
# deck-log kind (`changelog.d/sail-scheduling-is-a-state.md`). Only the rows named there moved:
# `agents/drive-captain.md`, `agents/sail-slice-watch.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the review cadence — once per slice over the whole diff, a return spot-checked and never
# reviewed (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-review-once-per-slice.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `agents/sail-review-mate.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the committed return — a shipwright hands back `commit <hash>` or `no commit`, and the session
# integrates the commit (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-a-return-is-a-commit.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `agents/sail-implement-shipwright.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for the fast checks per deployable (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-fast-checks-per-deployable.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `agents/sail-implement-shipwright.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
#
# Re-taken for mutation once per capability, bounded (`changelog.d/loop-cadence-mutation-once-per-capability.md`).
# Only the rows named there moved: `agents/sail-mutation-shipworm.md`. Every other row is still its earlier reading.
# 2026-10-14: every brief that runs a stage now names the skills that stage reads, and the quartermaster's
# substituted styling passage guards the two it names; the eleven briefs below moved for that edit alone
# (`changelog.d/agents-name-their-skills.md`).
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/capability-gates-once-per-capability.md: the rows for `agents/sail-adversary-privateer.md`, `agents/sail-converge-navigator.md`, `agents/sail-demo-hand.md`, `agents/sail-gaps-lookout.md`, `agents/sail-review-mate.md`, `agents/sail-slice-watch.md`, `agents/sail-tasks-quartermaster.md` moved, deliberately — converge, gaps, design review, adversary, mutation and the hand's walk run once per capability, and three of them moved off the slice.
# Re-taken 2026-10-17 for changelog.d/a-slice-carries-its-own-dispatch-line.md: only the rows for agents/sail-slice-watch.md moved, deliberately — a slice's dispatch line travels in its own pull request, and a delegate hands the diff review it cannot start back to the host.
